I would challenge the design put metadata like (environments , subsystems , business taxonomy , routing model) into separate fields in DB.
It makes db fields messy.
could we do this?:
1. use generated unique id as internal-id, use this for search (bigint type)
2. add a varchar internal-business-id named as (wallet-txn-id/ledger-txn-id or other name).
    internal-business-id = metadata + internal-id
    internal-business-id is used in business flow like logging, API, messaging.
    since internal-business-id contains internal-id, we can get an internal-id from it and search by internal-id.
    internal-business-id is also readable and contains virtual bucket info and env info.


I would challenge this:
    Keep bucket as a hint only.
For example, wallet-action is sharded by wallet-txn.internal-id, so that actions of one txn land into the same table.
When we get an action-id (internal-business-id) from upstream or log, we have to know which table contains that action,
and the only information is virtual bucket-no in action-id.
I don't think upstream should pass a bucket-no (which belongs to our logic) to us.